# .gitantivirusignore
# Paths (relative to repo root) to exclude from scanning.
# Lines beginning with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
# Trailing slashes and leading/trailing whitespace are stripped automatically.
# Forward slashes are treated as path separators on all platforms.

# These scanner source files contain regex pattern literals and recommendation
# strings that contain words like "eval(" or "password =" as part of their code,
# which would otherwise produce false-positive findings. Only these specific
# files are excluded; the rest of scanner/ and core/ are scanned normally.
scanner/code.js
scanner/packages.js

# Example config file — contains illustrative patterns, not real secrets
.gitantivirus.example.yml

# Test fixtures (known-bad files) are excluded from the production scan;
# a dedicated test step (npm test) verifies detection against them separately.
tests/malicious/
